prompt Keaton asked to confirm the three-body Cursor Grok premise, recommend a path, whether Cursor desktop can reach the Vultr pier over mosh or SSH with all code there, and whether fifty dollars a month overpays for that pier.
think Premise holds: pause Anthropic and OpenAI loops, three Cursor Grok bodies, one galaxy and two stars, xhigh unattended. Path keeps three clones and the Darwin/Linux split because AppKit and SkateCore still need a Mac and shared checkout reopened %291.
think Cursor desktop speaks Remote-SSH, not mosh. The pier already seats mosh plus tmux for cursor-agent terminals. Putting the GUI and three 24/7 agents on 8 GB with no swap was never measured; one Remote-SSH sitting into one clone plus Harvest is the honest diet.
think Vultr High Performance AMD 4 vCPU 8 GB 180 GB NVMe lists at 48 a month, the exact SKU on the card. Fifty is list plus rounding or add-ons, not a luxury SKU. The August study called 4/8 the soft up from the seated 2/4 value shelf; steal at 12 percent still does not earn dedicated.
obs All code on the pier as the only working tree would strand native-surface rungs. xy is already the ordering remote. The pier is the Linux houseplant floor, not the only houseplant.
